    "schemaxis.exiftool/1": {
      "guide": "docs/exiftool.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Read, audit and compare the metadata photographs declare about themselves. inventoryPhotos inventories fixed selected fields of 1 to 16 baseline JPEGs; the workbench family (inspectMetadata, auditMetadata, compareMetadata) reads up to 512 photos (JPEG, TIFF, DNG, PNG, WebP, HEIF) and XMP sidecars from an explicit list or a declared folder into 40 catalogued typed fields (capture times and offsets, device, exposure, description, rights, GPS location, orientation and frame size), with typed CSVs for Calc, per-source states, literal concordance, rule-based findings and baseline comparison. reconcileTime and locate analyse capture clocks and recorded positions; correctTime, setLocation and geotagFromTrack write new JPEG copies with corrected capture times, declared positions or positions interpolated on GPX tracks, from declared domain intent and an optional plan.",
        "assumptions": "Local regular JPEG (any coding process), TIFF, DNG, PNG, WebP and HEIF files (detected by signature, selected by suffix) and XMP sidecar files with stable IDs; synthetic or consented photographs only; ExifTool 13.55 (production) run by /usr/bin/perl with a clean environment and no configuration; metadata is observed and may be wrong; sources that disagree are reported, never resolved. Time and location workflows: references, assumed offsets, assumed-correct groups, positions, vertical references and track datums are the author's declarations and are never verified; no time zone or daylight-saving rule is known; GPX is untrusted XML.",
        "constraints": "1-512 items, <=64 MiB each (256 MiB for a TIFF or DNG) and <=1 GiB total; folder depth <=2 with <=4096 scanned entries and no symbolic link followed; the 40 catalogued fields only (everything else unassessed); no pixel decode; originals are never modified; new copies: every writing operation (editMetadata, removeMetadata, correctTime, setLocation, geotagFromTrack, copyMetadata, applySidecar) writes JPEG, TIFF, DNG, PNG and WebP files and edits the existing Exif and XMP items of HEIF files (HEIF item creation and HEIF removal and minimise are refused; minimise is offered for JPEG, PNG and WebP, thumbnails for JPEG only); the container-by-container field matrix is in docs/exiftool.md; no renaming, reverse geocoding, vertical datum conversion, ExifVersion promotion, raw tag, option or expression authoring or native geotagging; GPX tracks are 1 to 8 files of at most 32 MiB each (64 MiB in total) and are captured byte for byte; no MWG-compliance, datum conversion, WGS-84 inference or privacy certification; a Calc handoff needs the typed-table minimums (>=1 row, >=2 present values per number column).",
        "inspection": "Inspect metadata.json (per-item states, sources and reconciliation), manifest.json (every scanned entry with its inclusion reason), profile-<name>.csv, audit.json/findings.csv, comparison.json/differences.csv and, when requested, native-observations.json; retained captured files, native stdout and launchers stay in the run directory.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_PHOTO_SOURCE/PHOTO_HASH_MISMATCH/UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA: select a regular local image or XMP file and a matching pin. Container refusals (TIFF_UNKNOWN_OFFSET_SUSPECT, TIFF_LAYOUT_OVERLAP, PNG_METADATA_AFTER_IDAT, WEBP_LAYOUT_UNSUPPORTED, HEIF_IMPLIED_EXTENT, HEIF_METADATA_ITEM_CREATION_UNSUPPORTED, HEIF_REMOVAL_UNSUPPORTED, HEIF_EMPTY_METADATA_ITEM, IPTC_RESOURCE_TAIL_UNSUPPORTED, MINIMISE_UNSUPPORTED_CONTAINER and the other codes of containerprofiles.json) name the unsupported structure: that item is refused and keeps its outcome document. MEDIA_FOLDER_CHANGED: rerun when the folder is stable. NO_USABLE_ITEMS: open manifest.json for each item's fault. NATIVE_ANCHOR_MISMATCH: ExifTool and the independent reader disagree about that file; keep the evidence and do not publish its values. NATIVE_REPLAY_UNAVAILABLE: configure the pinned ExifTool 13.55 to verify native-observed values. Field-level unreadable, unsupported and ambiguous states carry a code and message on the source record. Legacy inventoryPhotos faults are unchanged: UNSUPPORTED_JPEG, DUPLICATE_EXIF_TAG, AMBIGUOUS_EXIF, INVALID_EXIF_STRUCTURE, INVALID_EXIF_VALUE, UNSUPPORTED_NATIVE_VERSION. Time and location: REFERENCE_INVALID, GROUP_MEMBERSHIP_INVALID, UNKNOWN_ITEM: fix the declaration named by the location. GROUP_CONFLICTING, ASSUMPTION_CONTRADICTED, REFERENCE_CONTRADICTED, DRIFT_IMPLAUSIBLE: the declared references disagree; reconcileTime lists every residual. TIME_SOURCES_CONFLICT, TIME_SOURCE_UNREADABLE, TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE, ALTITUDE_REFERENCE_NOT_EXPRESSIBLE, EXIF_CREATION_UNVERIFIED, ALTITUDE_MEANING_CHANGED: that item is refused or unchanged and keeps its artifact slot as an outcome document; read it. TRACK_DTD_REFUSED, TRACK_MALFORMED, TRACK_POINT_INVALID, TRACK_RESOURCE_LIMIT, TRACK_HASH_MISMATCH: repair or replace the GPX file. TRACK_NOT_COVERED, TRACK_OVERLAP_CONFLICT: the photo cannot be placed; widen maxGapSeconds or fix the clock only if that is true. PLAN_STALE, PLAN_INCONSISTENT, PLAN_CATALOGUE_UNKNOWN, CLOCK_PLAN_HASH_MISMATCH: regenerate the plan. CLOCK_CORRECTION_UNAVAILABLE: the clock-correction plan has no correction for that item; fix the plan."
      },
