        "lifecycle": {
          "timeout": "One total deadline covers capture, version, loader and module traces, both extraction processes and verification; CPU 300 s, address space 4GiB, file 16MiB and no core dumps per process, with the shared owned process-tree runner.",
          "cancellation": "Cancellation and deadline are checked before capture, between native stages and before publication; a live timeout and cancel were each observed against a genuine ExifTool 13.55 Perl process (its /proc exe is the system Perl and its argv names the ExifTool script and the captured inputs) after the launcher had written the input bindings; the qualifier-owned SIGSTOP is a race hold, and the qualifier requires the dispatch leader exit code -15 or -9, the PID and process group gone, a failed result, retained logs, no success publication or sidecar and that its own safety-net kill was not needed. The time and location writes (correctTime, setLocation, geotagFromTrack) have their own live lifecycle test: a genuine ExifTool Perl write process (argv recorded from /proc, including the empty -config argument) is held, its process group is ended with SIGKILL before cleanup, the process and group are gone, the run fails with no success publication and the test's own safety-net kill was not needed.",
          "logs": "Authored and effective plans, captured photos with identities, trusted launchers, input bindings, submissions, stdout/stderr, runtime file hashes and the receipt are retained.",
          "verification": "Offline: independent reader re-parses every retained photo, ExifTool JSON must equal the reader per selected tag with exact JSON types, the repeated fresh process must match byte for byte, every publication is rebuilt, and the receipt is rechecked."
        },
        "data": [
          {
            "id": "photos",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "image",
            "format": "JPEG",
            "traits": {
              "coding": "baseline sequential",
              "precision": "8-bit",
              "components": 3
            },
            "losses": [
